=== crafting
@title Choose Your Ingredients

~ var:first = item:iron-ore
~ var:second = item:charcoal

You set aside {var:first} and {var:second} for the smith.

* [Carry the ingredients to the forge] -> forge

=== forge
@title At the Forge

{if var:first == iron-ore}
The ore glows.
{/if}

You have {player:inventory:var:first:count} of the first ingredient
and {player:inventory:var:second:count} of the second.

{if player has var:first and player has var:second}
* [Combine {var:first} and {var:second}] { take player var:first; take player var:second; give player steel } -> smithy
{/if}
* [Leave the ingredients untouched] -> END

=== smithy
@title Steel

The smith hands you {item:steel}. Your chosen ingredients were
{var:first} and {var:second}; now neither remains in your inventory.

-> END
